/target
.DS_Store

# Design/process docs — kept locally for session continuity (STATUS.md is
# read at the start of every Claude session), not part of the public
# repo face. The root README is the one exception, once it exists.
*.md
!/README.md

# Secrets — never commit API keys/credentials (e.g. the Claude API key
# once that integration exists). Same convention already used for
# INSULA_SAFE_BROWSING_API_KEY: read from the environment, never hardcoded
# or checked in.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Test payloads used to live-test the sensor/auto-run pipeline against
# real file-encrypting behavior — functional, ~76MB self-contained .NET
# binaries. Deliberately included (not ignored) so anyone cloning the repo
# has a real ransomware-like sample to test Insula against — shipped with
# execute permission stripped (chmod a-x) as the safety default; see the
# README before touching them.
